## Scenarios

### compile-target environment facade contract

#### routes both entry-closure trace flags through the environment facade

- Verify: routes both entry-closure trace flags through the environment facade
   - Expected: env_set(flag, "1") is true
   - Expected: env_get(flag) ?? "" equals `"1")  # oracle: facade read observes the write`
   - Expected: env_set(flag, old) is true
   - Expected: env_get(flag) ?? "" equals `old)  # oracle: prior value restored`


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 11 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
# @req: REQ-GEN-APP-001
step("Verify: routes both entry-closure trace flags through the environment facade")
# Runtime oracle: the same facade the compile targets use (env_get/env_set)
# carries both trace flags in and out of this process environment.
val flags = ["SIMPLE_NATIVE_BUILD_TRACE_CLOSURE", "SIMPLE_NATIVE_BUILD_TRACE_CLOSURE_TIMING"]
for flag in flags:
    val old = env_get(flag) ?? ""
    expect(env_set(flag, "1")).to_equal(true)  # oracle: facade write succeeds
    expect(env_get(flag) ?? "").to_equal("1")  # oracle: facade read observes the write
    expect(env_set(flag, old)).to_equal(true)
    expect(env_get(flag) ?? "").to_equal(old)  # oracle: prior value restored
```

</details>

#### keeps adjacent native-build environment restoration on the same facade

- Verify: keeps adjacent native-build environment restoration on the same facade
   - Expected: env_set(key, "spec-probe") is true
   - Expected: env_get(key) ?? "" equals `"spec-probe")  # oracle: value exported`
   - Expected: env_set(key, old_value) is true
   - Expected: env_get(key) ?? "" equals `old_value)  # oracle: old value restored, not dropped`


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 11 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
# @req: REQ-GEN-APP-001
step("Verify: keeps adjacent native-build environment restoration on the same facade")
# Runtime oracle: the save/set/restore discipline the native-build path
# applies to its three environment variables works through the facade.
val keys = ["SIMPLE_OS_LOG_MODE", "SIMPLE_NATIVE_BUILD_TARGET", "SIMPLE_RUNTIME_PATH"]
for key in keys:
    val old_value = env_get(key) ?? ""
    expect(env_set(key, "spec-probe")).to_equal(true)
    expect(env_get(key) ?? "").to_equal("spec-probe")  # oracle: value exported
    expect(env_set(key, old_value)).to_equal(true)
    expect(env_get(key) ?? "").to_equal(old_value)  # oracle: old value restored, not dropped
```

</details>

